cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If the DECA theory, implementation, experiments, or research archive
  contributes to your work, please cite this repository and the ISCAS 2025
  ECA paper where appropriate.
type: software
title: >-
  Discriminative Energy Component Analysis: Optimal Commuting Measurements
  and Spectral Quadratic Classification
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Rongzhou
    alias: Lachlan Chen
repository-code: "https://github.com/lachlanchen/discriminative-energy-component-analysis"
url: "https://github.com/lachlanchen/discriminative-energy-component-analysis"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
abstract: >-
  A tested reformulation of Eigen-Component Analysis as constrained quantum
  state discrimination and structured quadratic classification. The release
  includes analytical results, a monotone Jacobi solver, SDP and PGM
  comparisons, Qiskit circuit simulations, public-data benchmarks, historical
  sources, and a compiled journal-style manuscript.
keywords:
  - eigen-component analysis
  - discriminative feature extraction
  - quadratic classification
  - joint diagonalization
  - quantum state discrimination
  - positive operator-valued measure
  - Qiskit
  - class-conditional second moments
  - commuting operators
  - quantum-inspired machine learning
  - subspace learning
